# X-Ray Crash Symbol Resolver (`xray-crash-symbol-resolver`)

When S.T.A.L.K.E.R. (X-Ray / OGSR Engine) crashes under Wine, Proton, or native Linux, it outputs stack trace crash dialogs or log entries with raw hexadecimal memory offsets:
`xrGame.dll + 0x3b4a12` or `CRASH: [00000001803b4a12]`.

Without symbol resolution, an AI agent must read 20–50 source files searching for function names or text fragments, burning **25,000 to 50,000 prompt tokens** on guesswork.

This skill runs fast, zero-token host CPU symbol resolution to translate raw crash offsets directly into exact source files and line numbers in under 20 milliseconds.

---

## 1. Symbol Resolution Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Raw Crash Offset: xrGame.dll+0x3b4a12"] --> B["Host Tool: addr2line / llvm-symbolizer / rizin"]
    B --> C["Resolved Coordinate: src/xrGame/alife_simulator.cpp#L184"]
    C --> D["Targeted Ingestion to Fable 5.1 (10 Lines only!)"]
```

---

## 2. Command Pipeline Standards

### A. For Linux Native & MinGW Builds with DWARF / PDB:
```bash
# Translates relative offset directly using addr2line
addr2line -e bin/xrGame.so -f -C 0x3b4a12
# Output:
# CALifeSimulator::update()
# /home/ericparsley/ogsr/src/xrGame/alife_simulator.cpp:184
```

### B. For Windows PE Binaries under Wine/Proton (with Symbols):
```bash
# Uses rizin or objdump to resolve function boundary & offset
rizin -q -c "s 0x3b4a12; af.; pdf" bin/xrGame.dll
```

### C. Output Format to Model:
Never dump disassembly pages into chat. Output the single resolved source coordinate:
```text
#CRASH_COORDINATE:
BINARY: bin/xrGame.dll (RVA: 0x3b4a12)
FUNCTION: CALifeSimulator::update()
SOURCE: src/xrGame/alife_simulator.cpp#L184
FAULT_TYPE: ACCESS_VIOLATION_READ (0x0000000000000018)
```

---

## 3. Quota & Context Savings

- **Eliminates Blind File Exploration:** Resolves the exact line in 15ms on the host before making an LLM tool call.
- **Precision Focus:** Fable 5.1 reads only the 15-line block around `alife_simulator.cpp#L184` instead of ingesting the entire 2,000-line translation unit.
- **Saves ~30,000 tokens** per crash triage cycle.
